{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_vltcif34zfaytv3qbbqpmrd7gsb3vgdbafzdn6em5eyehe6wxsqq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Rust 1.94 inserts a debug-mode null-deref check on *any* raw pointer deref. I'll read the struct image through libc's `memcpy` — an opaque extern call carries no Rust-level checks, exactly like a C load:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":594,"cache_read_input_tokens":90715,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":594,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d3d04f41-b20c-47bc-b061-46285585259e","uuid":"7e6a825b-3043-4323-92e1-921eabde48a3","timestamp":"2026-08-18T09:23:59.892Z"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_vltcif34zfaytv3qbbqpmrd7gsb3vgdbafzdn6em5eyehe6wxsqq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_0158GPVzkuVoH2eCV1tJqcP4","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-RZqsPe/translated_rust/src/lib.rs","old_string":"/// The members are read one byte at a time through a `*const u8` rather than\n/// via a `&foo_t` reference or `ptr::read_unaligned`. Both alternatives add\n/// checks that the C does not have, and each was observed to diverge:\n///\n/// * forming `&*foo` trips Rust's \"misaligned pointer dereference\" check, but\n///   the C applies no alignment requirement and x86-64 loads unaligned\n///   addresses fine, so C happily prints for a misaligned `foo_t *`;\n/// * `ptr::read_unaligned` carries a debug-only `unsafe precondition` that the\n///   pointer is non-null, which aborts with `SIGABRT`, whereas the C's\n///   unchecked dereference of `NULL` raises `SIGSEGV`.\n///\n/// A plain `u8` load has alignment 1 and no null precondition, so it compiles\n/// to a bare `mov` that faults exactly like the C does and tolerates any\n/// alignment. `from_ne_bytes` then reassembles `z` in the target's native byte\n/// order, matching the C's native `int` load.\n#[unsafe(no_mangle)]\npub unsafe extern \"C\" fn print_foo(foo: *const foo_t) {\n    let base = foo as *const u8;\n    let bits = *base;\n    let z_at = base.add(core::mem::offset_of!(foo_t, z));\n    let z = c_int::from_ne_bytes([*z_at, *z_at.add(1), *z_at.add(2), *z_at.add(3)]);","new_string":"/// The struct image is fetched with libc's `memcpy` rather than by\n/// dereferencing a Rust pointer or reference. Every Rust-level read adds a\n/// check the C does not have, and each alternative was observed to diverge from\n/// the C library:\n///\n/// * forming `&*foo` trips the \"misaligned pointer dereference\" check and\n///   aborts, but the C applies no alignment requirement and x86-64 loads\n///   unaligned addresses fine, so the C prints normally for a misaligned\n///   `foo_t *`;\n/// * `ptr::read_unaligned` carries a debug-only `unsafe precondition` that the\n///   pointer is non-null, and a plain `*ptr` deref carries a debug-only null\n///   check; both abort with `SIGABRT`, whereas the C's unchecked dereference of\n///   `NULL` raises `SIGSEGV`.\n///\n/// An opaque `extern \"C\"` call performs none of those checks, so it faults\n/// exactly where and how the C does and tolerates any alignment.\n/// `from_ne_bytes` then reassembles `z` in the target's native byte order,\n/// matching the C's native `int` load.\n#[unsafe(no_mangle)]\npub unsafe extern \"C\" fn print_foo(foo: *const foo_t) {\n    const N: usize = core::mem::size_of::<foo_t>();\n    const Z: usize = core::mem::offset_of!(foo_t, z);\n\n    let mut img = [0u8; N];\n    memcpy(\n        img.as_mut_ptr() as *mut c_void,\n        foo as *const c_void,\n        N,\n    );\n\n    let bits = img[0];\n    let z = c_int::from_ne_bytes([img[Z], img[Z + 1], img[Z + 2], img[Z + 3]]);"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":594,"cache_read_input_tokens":90715,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":594,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d3d04f41-b20c-47bc-b061-46285585259e","uuid":"282e8fc0-6021-45d3-9e0d-fe7305e08ed0","timestamp":"2026-08-18T09:24:10.636Z"}
