r read path (`&*p`, `read_unaligned`, plain `*p`).\n\nFixed by fetching the struct image via libc `memcpy` — an opaque `extern \"C\"` call carrying none of those checks, so it faults exactly where and how C does. Notably this was a **debug-only** divergence, invisible if only the optimized artifact were tested.\n\n## Two harness bugs worth flagging\n- `cargo test` never builds the `cdylib` (no `rlib` ⇒ tests don't link it), so a stale or absent `.so` would have been silently verified. The harness now builds it into a separate `--target-dir` (cargo's build lock is per target dir).\n- My first capture implementation redirected fd 1 in-process, which swallowed libtest's own `test … ok` progress lines and produced spurious line-shifted \"diffs.\" Captures now run in a forked child, which also gives crash isolation for free.\n\n## Anti-vacuous-pass check\nPassing tests prove nothing unless they can fail, so I mutation-tested the suite: 9 single-edit mutations to `src/lib.rs`; **8 caught** (7–15 tests each). The lone survivor — `%u`→`%d` on `x` — I verified is a *semantically equivalent* mutant, not a gap: `x` is masked to 2 bits and `printf` renders 0–3 identically under both.\n\n## Completion gate\n- ✅ `nm -D`: 0 missing symbols; `ldd -r` shows 0 unresolved.\n- ✅ All 15 `CONFIGS.md` rows pass across randomized inputs (fixed seed).\n- ✅ All 12 `ERRORS.md` rows pass, comparing the exact terminating signal — not merely \"both failed.\"\n- ✅ Holds under every feature combination. `Cargo.toml` declares **no `[features]`**, so there is exactly one; I additionally ran the full matrix against both the debug and release profiles, which is what exposed bug #2.\n\n`c_src` is untouched (sources retain original mtimes; only the prescribed `build/` was added). `./verify_all.sh` reproduces the entire matrix and exits 0."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":808,"cache_read_input_tokens":122136,"cache_crea